<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Admirable Campaign</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venezuelan-war-of-independence">Venezuelan War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Admirable Campaign was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>'s military campaign of 1813 in which he advanced from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> across the Andes into western Venezuela and drove back the royalists in a series of victories. During the march he issued the Decree of War to the Death at Trujillo in June. He entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> in August 1813, restoring republican rule as the Second Republic of Venezuela, and was acclaimed as the Liberator.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/admirable-campaign.jpg" alt="Admirable Campaign" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C arango · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Campanna_Admirable.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
